diff --git a/CONTEXT.md b/CONTEXT.md
index 7a781380..d3bfd2e5 100644
--- a/CONTEXT.md
+++ b/CONTEXT.md
@@ -28,6 +28,10 @@ _Avoid_: demo sketch; calling it a stock Pattern (stock Patterns are Pixelblaze)
 How a **FastLED Pattern**'s own LEDs reach the map's pixels. *Index*: map pixel i shows `leds[i]` (strips; sketches that follow the map size through `PXLBLZ_NUM_LEDS`). *Surface* ("Fläche"): the sketch keeps its own NUM_LEDS and raster; every map pixel takes the bytes of the sketch LED nearest to its 2D map position (no blending, so the bytes stay FastLED's), with Contain/Fill fit, optional flips and, for 3D maps, an axis pair. The sketch raster comes from the sketch's FastLED screen map, else the example catalogue's width×height, else a square guess. Automatic unless chosen: surface for a 2D/3D sketch on a ≥2D map whose LED count differs from the map's. Stored as `// @pxlblz-projection …` in an editable Pattern's header (never compiled) or in a read-only example's per-demo overrides.
 _Avoid_: mapping (a **Map** is the coordinate set), resampling/scaling (nothing is interpolated).
 
+**Active mask** (local fork):
+Per-slot flag of an installation **Map** (one entry per point, in map order): 1 = the slot has a real LED position, 0 = it has none (TouchDesigner active mask = 0; the export parks such slots at one coordinate). Every Pattern (Pixelblaze and FastLED) still runs for masked slots — render functions are called for every index — but their output is forced to black in the preview and in the router frame, they are not drawn, and they do not count towards a **FastLED projection** surface fit. Stored on the map record as `importMetadata.activeMask` (compact run-length form); a mask whose length differs from the map's point count is ignored with a warning. The deck shows "Maske: N aktiv / M ausgeblendet".
+_Avoid_: hiding pixels (they still exist, keep their index and are routed — just always black); calling the mask a Map or a route filter.
+
 **FastLED compile service**:
 The local helper (`fastled-integration/service/server.mjs`, default `http://127.0.0.1:9996`) that turns FastLED Pattern source plus defines (`PXLBLZ_NUM_LEDS` = the map's pixel count) into a wasm module and compiler diagnostics. Started by the Art-Net launcher; when it is not reachable the preview says so and the editor keeps saving.
 
