 - Projection (`src/engine/fastled/fastledProjection.ts`, deck section "FastLED" in `FastLedProjectionPanel.tsx`): *index* keeps `leds[i]` → map index i and passes `PXLBLZ_NUM_LEDS` = map pixel count; *surface* compiles without PXLBLZ defines (the sketch keeps its NUM_LEDS) and gives the handle a precomputed table map index → sketch LED (−1 = black), so `render*(i)` emits the L2/L1 bytes of `table[i]` and the packed frame keeps the map's pixel count (router frame size unchanged). Sketch positions: the sketch's screen maps (`getScreenMaps()`, host export `pxl_screenmap_json`, sent by the worker with `started`/changed frames; serpentine/XYMap already applied), else the catalogue `geometry` width×height row-major (serpentine when the source declares `kMatrixSerpentineLayout = true`/`SERPENTINE true`; a clone finds its example by the provenance header), else a square guess with a deck notice. Map positions: each pixel's `sample` (2D: x,y; 3D: chosen axis pair, default the two largest extents), fitted onto the sketch bounds padded by half an LED (Contain: uniform scale, whole map inside the sketch; Fill: per axis), optional flips; nearest sketch LED within one LED pitch via a bucket grid, ties → lower index; memoised per (map points, sketch layout, options), ~ms for 10,330 pixels. Automatic choice: surface for `@pxlblz-dim` ≥ 2 on a ≥2D map unless the source uses `PXLBLZ_NUM_LEDS/WIDTH/HEIGHT` or the known LED count (catalogue, or after start) equals the map's. Persistence: `// @pxlblz-projection [index|surface] [fit=fill] [flip=x|y|xy] [axes=xy|xz|yz]` in an editable Pattern's header; the compile request blanks that line and the artifact cache key drops it, so a projection change never recompiles. Read-only examples store the same text as `fastledProjection` in their `demoOverrides` bag (cleared by "Revert to recommended"); Clone writes it into the copy's header.
+- Active mask (`src/engine/maps/activeMask.ts`, all Patterns, not only FastLED): a custom map record may carry `importMetadata.activeMask = { version: 1, encoding: 'rle01', count, first, runs, active, source?, fingerprint?, updatedAt? }` — alternating run lengths starting with value `first`, summing to `count`; `active` and `fingerprint` (`fnv1a32:` over the 0/1 bytes) are checked on decode. Stored in the existing `import_metadata_json` column (no migration; `PATCH /api/maps/:id` already writes `importMetadata` as a whole). A map whose metadata has no Controller provenance uses `kind: 'installation'`; only `kind: 'controller'` (`isControllerMapImport`) makes a map frozen or shows the "Imported" facts. `mapFromRecord` validates the mask against the point count (wrong length or malformed → ignored, `console.warn` and an amber deck/map-pane warning) and puts it on the `PixelMap`; `resolveLayout` returns `activeMask` (per pixel index, active past the baked array, null when nothing is masked) plus the summary. `createRenderLoop({ activeMask })` still calls `render*` for every index (Pattern state and determinism unchanged) and writes black for masked indices into the packed frame / pixel list, so preview and `externalPixelOutput` (router) get black there and unchanged bytes elsewhere. `Preview.tsx` hands the renderer only the active indices (positions, normals, and a compacted copy of each frame), so the parked cluster is neither drawn nor part of the measured bounds/spacing. The FastLED surface table gets `active`: masked points → −1 and excluded from the map bounds (Contain/Fill fit only real LED positions) and from the automatic 3D axis choice. Deck: "Maske: 6.962 aktiv / 3.368 ausgeblendet" (`editorStore.activeMaskLabel`); map pane fact row "Maske". Set/clear a mask with `node scripts/set-map-active-mask.mjs --map <id> --mask <0/1 JSON array>` (local dev session, merges with existing metadata, verifies after writing). Not applied yet: Shows, Gallery thumbnails, Controller (hardware) export.
 - Preview start: the deck pauses itself while no Pattern is loaded (upstream #478); it now resumes when the pause was automatic and a Pattern arrives (cold load, deep link), while a user pause stays.
 - Controls: FastLED UI elements map to ranged slider/toggle Controls (`PatternMetadata.controls[].range`); values persist in `PatternRecord.controls` (`controls_json`) keyed by UI name.
 - Worker and watchdog: the worker runs the same host calls in the same order, so bytes are identical; frames are pipelined by one IDE frame (frame(dt_k) requests frame k while frame k-1 is shown; a late answer repeats the last frame and the deltas accumulate). No answer within 2 s (setup 10 s) terminates the worker: runtime error, last frame kept. The host's loop/show budget still reports runaway loops that call `millis/delay/show` (they keep running). Measured at 4,593 LEDs: ~1 ms per frame in the worker, ~1.4 ms round trip, main-thread cost ~0.1 ms per frame; added latency one IDE frame.
diff --git a/scripts/set-map-active-mask.mjs b/scripts/set-map-active-mask.mjs
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..207b77aa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/set-map-active-mask.mjs
@@ -0,0 +1,146 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env node
+// Sets (or clears) the active mask of one map through the local PXLBLZ API.
+//
+//   node scripts/set-map-active-mask.mjs --map <mapId> --mask <mask.json> [options]
+//
+// <mask.json>: a JSON array of 0/1 (one entry per map slot, in map order), or an
+// object with such an array under `mask`, `activeMask` or `active`.
+//
+// Options:
+//   --ide-url <url>    Local IDE/API origin (default http://localhost:5175; only
+//                      localhost / 127.0.0.1 allowed).
+//   --dev-vars <path>  .dev.vars holding the API's SESSION_SECRET (default
+//                      E:/PXLBLZ-ArtNet/PXLBLZ-IDE-main/.dev.vars - the checkout
+//                      that serves the API on 5174).
+//   --source <text>    Provenance stored with the mask (default touchdesigner).
+//   --dry-run          Validate and print what would be written; no PATCH.
+//   --clear            Remove the mask (keeps other importMetadata fields).
+//
+// Same local-dev session approach as pxlblz_manager's ide(): a session token for
+// the provisioned local developer identity is minted from SESSION_SECRET with
+// the IDE's own createSessionToken (no browser cookie). The mask is stored as
+// `importMetadata.activeMask` (rle01, see src/engine/maps/activeMask.ts); other
+// importMetadata fields are kept. PATCH /api/maps/:id replaces the whole
+// importMetadata column, so the script merges with the current value first.
+import fs from 'node:fs'
+import path from 'node:path'
+import assert from 'node:assert/strict'
+import { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from 'node:url'
+
+const ROOT = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..')
+
+function parseArgs(argv) {
+  const out = { ideUrl: 'http://localhost:5175', devVars: 'E:/PXLBLZ-ArtNet/PXLBLZ-IDE-main/.dev.vars', source: 'touchdesigner', dryRun: false, clear: false }
+  for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i++) {
+    const a = argv[i]
+    const next = () => {
+      const v = argv[++i]
+      if (v === undefined) throw new Error(`${a} needs a value`)
+      return v
+    }
+    if (a === '--map') out.map = next()
+    else if (a === '--mask') out.mask = next()
+    else if (a === '--ide-url') out.ideUrl = next()
+    else if (a === '--dev-vars') out.devVars = next()
+    else if (a === '--source') out.source = next()
+    else if (a === '--dry-run') out.dryRun = true
+    else if (a === '--clear') out.clear = true
+    else if (a === '-h' || a === '--help') out.help = true
+    else throw new Error(`unknown argument ${a}`)
+  }
+  return out
+}
+
+function readMaskFile(file) {
+  const value = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8').replace(/^\uFEFF/, ''))
+  const arr = Array.isArray(value) ? value : value?.mask ?? value?.activeMask ?? value?.active
+  if (!Array.isArray(arr)) throw new Error(`${file}: expected a JSON array of 0/1 (or {mask:[...]})`)
+  arr.forEach((v, i) => {
+    if (!(v === 0 || v === 1 || v === true || v === false)) throw new Error(`${file}: entry ${i} is ${JSON.stringify(v)}, expected 0 or 1`)
+  })
+  return arr.map((v) => (v ? 1 : 0))
+}
+
+async function session(ideUrl, devVarsPath) {
+  assert(['localhost', '127.0.0.1'].includes(new URL(ideUrl).hostname), 'Only a local IDE instance is allowed')
+  const vars = fs.readFileSync(devVarsPath, 'utf8')
+  const match = vars.match(/^\s*SESSION_SECRET\s*=\s*(.+?)\s*$/m)
+  assert(match, `SESSION_SECRET missing in ${devVarsPath}`)
+  const secret = match[1].replace(/^(['"])(.*)\1$/, '$2')
+  const { createSessionToken } = await import(pathToFileURL(path.join(ROOT, 'src/cloudflare/auth.ts')).href)
+  const token = await createSessionToken({
+    userId: 'github:local-dev', primaryProvider: 'github', primaryHandle: 'local-dev',
+    githubUserId: 'local-dev', githubLogin: 'local-dev', displayName: 'Local Dev', avatarUrl: null,
+  }, secret)
+  return async (endpoint, { method = 'GET', body } = {}) => {
+    const response = await fetch(ideUrl.replace(/\/+$/, '') + endpoint, {
+      method,
+      headers: { Cookie: 'pxlblz_session=' + encodeURIComponent(token), ...(body === undefined ? {} : { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }) },
+      ...(body === undefined ? {} : { body: JSON.stringify(body) }),
+      signal: AbortSignal.timeout(30000),
+    })
+    const text = await response.text()
+    let value
+    try { value = JSON.parse(text) } catch { throw new Error(`Invalid response: HTTP ${response.status}`) }
+    if (!response.ok || value.ok === false) throw new Error(value.error || `HTTP ${response.status}`)
+    return value
+  }
+}
+
+async function main() {
+  const args = parseArgs(process.argv.slice(2))
+  if (args.help || !args.map || (!args.mask && !args.clear)) {
+    console.log('usage: node scripts/set-map-active-mask.mjs --map <mapId> (--mask <mask.json> | --clear) [--ide-url URL] [--dev-vars PATH] [--source TEXT] [--dry-run]')
+    process.exit(args.help ? 0 : 2)
+  }
+  const { encodeActiveMask, decodeActiveMask, formatActiveMaskSummary } = await import(pathToFileURL(path.join(ROOT, 'src/engine/maps/activeMask.ts')).href)
+  const api = await session(args.ideUrl, args.devVars)
+
+  const { maps } = await api('/api/maps')
+  const map = maps.find((m) => m.id === args.map)
+  if (!map) throw new Error(`map ${args.map} not found (${maps.length} maps)`)
+  const pointCount = Array.isArray(map.points) ? map.points.length : 0
+  console.log(`map: ${map.name} (${map.id}), dim ${map.dim}, ${pointCount} points, generator ${map.generator}`)
+  const existing = map.importMetadata && typeof map.importMetadata === 'object' ? map.importMetadata : null
+  console.log(`current importMetadata: ${existing ? `kind=${existing.kind ?? '(none)'}${existing.activeMask ? `, activeMask ${existing.activeMask.active}/${existing.activeMask.count}` : ', no activeMask'}` : 'none'}`)
+
+  let importMetadata
+  if (args.clear) {
+    if (!existing?.activeMask) { console.log('nothing to clear'); return }
+    const { activeMask: _drop, ...rest } = existing
+    // A metadata object that only carried the mask goes away entirely (null).
+    importMetadata = rest.kind === 'controller' || Object.keys(rest).some((k) => k !== 'kind' && k !== 'source') ? rest : null
+    console.log('clearing activeMask')
+  } else {
+    const bits = readMaskFile(args.mask)
+    if (bits.length !== pointCount) {
+      throw new Error(`mask has ${bits.length} entries but the map has ${pointCount} points - not written`)
+    }
+    const activeMask = encodeActiveMask(bits, { source: args.source, updatedAt: Date.now() })
+    // Self-check: the stored form decodes back to the same bits.
+    const back = decodeActiveMask(JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(activeMask)))
+    assert(back.length === bits.length && back.every((v, i) => v === bits[i]), 'rle01 round trip failed')
+    importMetadata = existing ? { ...existing, activeMask } : { kind: 'installation', source: args.source, activeMask }
+    console.log(`mask: ${formatActiveMaskSummary(activeMask.active, activeMask.count - activeMask.active)}, ${activeMask.runs.length} runs, ${JSON.stringify(activeMask).length} bytes, ${activeMask.fingerprint}`)
+  }
+
+  if (args.dryRun) {
+    console.log('dry run - nothing written')
+    return
+  }
+  await api(`/api/maps/${encodeURIComponent(map.id)}`, { method: 'PATCH', body: { importMetadata, updatedAt: Date.now() } })
+  const after = (await api('/api/maps')).maps.find((m) => m.id === map.id)
+  const stored = after?.importMetadata?.activeMask
+  if (args.clear) {
+    assert(!stored, 'mask still present after clear')
+    console.log('cleared. Reload the IDE tab to pick it up.')
+  } else {
+    assert(stored && stored.fingerprint === importMetadata.activeMask.fingerprint, 'stored mask does not match')
+    console.log('written and verified. Reload the IDE tab to pick it up.')
+  }
+}
+
+main().catch((err) => {
+  console.error(`error: ${err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)}`)
+  process.exit(1)
+})
